    function testFuzz_property(address currentOwner, address newOwner) public {
        // avoid the zero address for currentOwner so we can prank from it realistically
        vm.assume(currentOwner != address(0));
        // ensure newOwner can be any address (including zero) — no further restriction

        // Arrange: set contract owner to currentOwner by directly calling transferOwnership from the deployer
        // As the newly deployed contract's owner is initially address(0) (default), we need to set owner.
        // We'll first impersonate address(0) to set owner to currentOwner if allowed; but only owner can call transferOwnership.
        // Instead, we simulate proper initialisation: deployer sets owner to currentOwner by calling transferOwnership
        // Deployer must be owner for that; since owner is zero, many contracts allow setting from zero. To make this universal
        // and independent of that, we will directly set up by using a low-level approach: we will first set owner to address(this)
        // by calling transferOwnership while pranked as address(this) if allowed. But initially owner == address(0), so onlyOwner would fail.
